{"title":"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2d","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three players, Ava, Beau, and Cato, are playing a tournament. Each person plays exactly two games, one game against each of the other players. If a game ends in a tie, both players are awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. Otherwise, the winning player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> points and the losing player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points.\n</p><p>For example, if the tournament results are as shown below and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129a394e53ae5d9485467a5da722ed2d61c63077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 2$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, then points are awarded as follows:\n</p><p>(add a table to the Problem 2 page)\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the sum of the points that have been awarded to the three players when the tournament has finished. In the example above, Ava is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point, Beau is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, and Cato is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae948412b3206828fd197dbd41fd8a41bf7c4de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> in the example.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the tournament finishes with exactly one of the three games ending in a tie. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/24468ae0baa4e779a1f7de485331e5dc0ce74b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of games where one person won and the other person lost. The tournament had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games in total, so there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb8669416734fe4922ed96d667085f95722d6bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 - g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> games where both people tied.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people are involved in each game and each person gains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point from a game where someone tied, the total number of points increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34a068fc593714a83c298e0e3570977270c1c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> every time a game is tied.\n</p><p>Because the winning person gains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> points while the losing person gains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points in a game where one person won and the other lost, the total number of points increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647b24699730c2a6dbe787f5052e16f0e0149d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W + 0 = W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> every time a game is won by someone.\n</p><p>Thus, we can set up an equation using all of the information:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff9acd154f86a2734ea06e1972a8fa5b8e71a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(3 - g) + Wg = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can distribute:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411d56e4c051bba19b748665ad47a8bafceda35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 - 2 \\times g + Wg = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71d54d6b6be96ab8e7a5b7d3be0812739232facf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 2g + Wg = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b3ad42e917d173e30520119fdad057d175bbab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(W - 2) + 6 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f64f9c2b85f3b8843449e55983b46b1970dbd0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(W - 2) = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games total, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a non-negative integer. Using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ecb6fe33233817abc30314d057da68dc44c9fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 = 3 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee8ac1ef24a64e6d99b4e46c05a8ecabfdda486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2f01920d45b7156d625b28cfe31354c89d5af4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W - 2 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65812d9c8a6cc32cd0aff6e6080c9e011f28e608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac57b23f73332f4a97b97cfb54631422e897d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W - 2 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee8ac1ef24a64e6d99b4e46c05a8ecabfdda486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca99181c60c512d59d07b7349779e818999ff2bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65812d9c8a6cc32cd0aff6e6080c9e011f28e608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9cad68331c37e2d1a6adef53ad1361ab306526f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca99181c60c512d59d07b7349779e818999ff2bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9cad68331c37e2d1a6adef53ad1361ab306526f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018031931\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 134/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1050/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7012/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.603      1 2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    8.603      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35039:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018031931 and revision id 272003. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}